# FEAT: PIN THIS
Q14 - Wipe timing nuance: eager wipe at lapse has one consequence you should sign off on — you're reading a recipe/answer from across the room, 10 minutes pass, and the feed (including the idle-screen digest) empties while you look at it. Eager wipe on a timer anyway, or lazy wipe (content stays until your next command, but boot never hydrates a lapsed session)?
Eager wipe. Your rule is "only the current session renders," and the 10-min window is the grace period; if an answer needs to outlive it, that's a future "pin this" feature, not a reason to render stale sessions.


